    "content": "Somali Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre has appointed Abdulqadir Omar Macalin as the new Minister of Ports and Marine Transport, according to a statement from the Prime Minister's office. The appointment was made in accordance with Article 120, paragraphs 2 and 3, of the Provisional Constitution of the Federal Republic of Somalia.\n\nThe statement said the Prime Minister considered Macalin's biography, education, and professional experience in making the appointment. It also noted that the Prime Minister took into account the advice of the President of the Federal Republic of Somalia.\n\nMacalin replaces the previous minister, whose tenure saw ongoing efforts to develop Somalia's port infrastructure and maritime sector. The ports ministry oversees key facilities such as the Port of Mogadishu, which serves as a vital gateway for trade and humanitarian supplies.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the appointment is significant because ports and marine transport are central to the country's economic links with the outside world. Many diaspora members are involved in shipping, import-export businesses, and humanitarian logistics that depend on efficient port operations. The new minister's background and policies will be closely watched by these communities.\n\nThe appointment comes as the federal government continues to prioritize economic development and security, with ports playing a key role in generating revenue and facilitating trade. The international community and diaspora investors have shown interest in Somalia's maritime potential.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/18/raiisulwasaare-xamse-oo-wasiir-cusub-u-magacaabay-wasaaradda-dekedaha/",
